installation :xincheng_yard do
  name "The Xincheng Yard"
  aka "新城场"
  tags :biotech, :symbiosis, :legibility
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    A walled yard among the tomb mounds outside Xincheng, east of Jiayuguan, where the #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeepers"} challenge a #{ref :severed_strains, "severed strain"} before its card is renewed. The site was chosen for its edge. Irrigation reaches this far, so a neighbourhood network's hedge stands within thirty metres of the cells, while the yard's own ground is kiln-fired brick, salted gravel and nothing else.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :structure, heading: "Eight Cells"
    Eight brick cells open at the top, each holding one bed on a fired ceramic stand. Distances from the hedge are marked on the ground in whitewash at five, fifteen and thirty metres, and a cell can be worked at any of the three. Nothing in the yard is alive except the beds, the hedge and the people; the stands, barrows, trays, gloves and cuffs are all #{ref :sterile_machines, "built to come apart and be baked"}.

    The case shelf is a single ledger of cards and a rack of #{ref :gate_moss, "gate-moss"} plates cut from the same beds the crossings use.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :operations, heading: "A Trace"
    A bed reaching the end of its four-month cycle is carried out, stood at its marked distance and left four days. Twice a day someone walks the joins at the pace the #{ref :the_seam_pass, "procedure"} fixes — stand foot, cell drain, barrow tray, gloves, cuffs — pressing a plate to each and reading it a quarter of an hour later.

    A bed that reaches the hedge fails. So does a bed that stays grey while a barrow tray goes black, and that failure is entered against the tray rather than against the strain. Every bed the yard challenges is broken afterwards, so the yard consumes eight beds a cycle, and its throughput sets how many lineages can hold a current card at any time. #{ref :the_gate_schedule, "The gate schedule"} prices a crossing on an expired card at the lineage-audit rate per documented generation, which is why the waiting list for the yard is kept by the clerks who keep the fee trays.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "Four Days At Five Metres"
    The card says four days at five metres. A strain that cannot reach a hedge in four days may reach something else in a season, and the yard has no way to run a season.

    What it has is arithmetic. A #{ref :the_season_credit, "credit"} bought off a winter held four days' carry above a Himalayan intake says how much of a season four days accounts for, for one class of bed, and a renewal that carries a credit line renews longer than one that does not. Eleven of the yard's renewals in 2085 carried one. #{ref :the_borrowed_season, "The Borrowed Season"} is what seven of those eleven cost, and it is the reason the line now names a class.

    #{ref :the_preservationists, "Preservationist"} couriers have asked in writing why the trace is renewed rather than lengthened. The answer entered on the form is the throughput figure. A bed pulled early reads slowly here as it does at a crossing, and a contested plate in the yard costs the lineage its whole cycle.
  PROSE
end
